An example of a valid CSS rule would be:

```css
body {
  font-size: 16px;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  background-color: #f1f1f1;
}
```

This CSS rule is targeting the `body` element of an HTML document, and applying several styles to it. It sets the font size to 16 pixels, the font family to Arial or sans-serif, removes any margin or padding around the element, and sets the background color to a light gray.
